Modification notice:
  This fork uses the visible product branding LayerLab and includes
  local changes for higher-quality stem separation, FFmpeg handling, UI
  styling, asynchronous queue handling, bass dropout repair, and
  phase-coherence repair. Additional changes include optional per-stem denoise,
  progress/ETA surfacing, responsive neon UI refinements, desktop runtime
  setup hardening, conservative cleanup/maintenance helpers, fork-separated
  desktop storage paths, fork release update URLs, and optional release
  signing/notarization hooks. WAV/PCM gating, DC/peak stabilization, RMS, and
  waveform peak generation can run in a bundled Rust sidecar, while Demucs
  models can remain loaded in bounded persistent worker processes between jobs.
  See the Git history for the complete change record.

Third-party dependencies:
  Runtime dependencies remain licensed by their respective authors. Packaged
  builds include THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, and
  THIRD_PARTY_INVENTORY.json generated from the exact packaged Python runtime
  and target-specific Rust dependency graph.

Model-weight distinction:
  Demucs source code is MIT-licensed. Demucs maintainers state that the
  published pretrained weights are not covered by that MIT license and are
  provided for personal/research usage. LayerLab does not bundle those weights;
  downloading them on first use does not grant additional rights.

FFmpeg distribution:
  Packaged LayerLab runtimes remove the GPL-enabled FFmpeg executable embedded
  in imageio-ffmpeg wheels. Desktop setup downloads the disclosed build
  directly from its provider. Mirroring or rebundling that executable requires
  compliance with the exact build's GPL/LGPL and corresponding-source terms.

Additional runtime helper:
  imageio-ffmpeg
  https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg
  License: BSD-2-Clause
  Used to locate an FFmpeg executable. Public desktop runtime builds remove the
  GPL-enabled executable embedded in its wheel and use the separately disclosed
  first-run FFmpeg download instead.

  Hound
  https://github.com/ruuda/hound
  License: Apache-2.0
  Used by the bundled Rust `layerlab-pcm` sidecar to read and write PCM16,
  PCM24, PCM32, and float32 WAV files for post-separation processing.

Music-analysis components:
  Beat This!
  https://github.com/CPJKU/beat_this
  License: MIT (source code and published model weights)
  Used for neural beat and downbeat detection in all analysis profiles, with
  a librosa fallback when the model is unavailable.

  music21
  https://github.com/cuthbertLab/music21
  License: BSD-3-Clause
  Used to validate generated Standard MIDI files and produce key, pitch-range,
  and Roman-numeral harmonic summaries.

Development-only evaluation component:
  mir_eval
  https://github.com/mir-evaluation/mir_eval
  License: MIT
  Used by the optional labelled-chord benchmark to calculate WCSR and
  segmentation metrics. It is not bundled in public desktop runtimes.
